//@version=6
// @description ⚠️ DEPRECATED: This library is no longer maintained and should not be used in new work.
// @description As of 2026-01-23, this library is deprecated. If you imported it by version, stop using this version and migrate.
// @description Notes: Public library publications can’t be “deleted” after the publish window; deprecation is the practical option.

// IMPORTANT
// 1) Keep the library() title EXACTLY the same as your existing published library name.
// 2) Update the replacement placeholder below.
// 3) Publish this as a NEW VERSION of the library.

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Library declaration
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// KEEP THIS NAME EXACTLY THE SAME AS YOUR CURRENT LIBRARY NAME:

library("QTCore", overlay=false)

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Deprecation message (edit these)
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
const string _REPLACEMENT = "<PASTE_REPLACEMENT_LINK_OR_IMPORT_PATH_HERE>"
const string _MSG =
     "DEPRECATED: This library is no longer maintained (deprecated on 2026-01-23).\n"
   + "Do not use this library in new scripts.\n"
   + "Replacement: " + _REPLACEMENT + "\n"
   + "If you are importing this library already, pin your import to the last working version you trust and migrate off it."

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Exported helpers
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// @function Returns the deprecation notice string. (Safe to call; does not halt execution.)
// @returns The deprecation message.
export deprecated_message() =>
    _MSG

// @function Call this at the top of any script that imports this library if you want it to hard-stop.
// @returns The same deprecation message (unreachable after the error, but required for return typing).
export deprecated_guard() =>
    runtime.error(_MSG)
    _MSG

// @function Library version label for humans.
// @returns A simple version label.
export deprecated_version() =>
    "DEPRECATED (2026-01-23)"

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// OPTIONAL: If you want this version to ALWAYS fail whenever it is imported,
// uncomment the next two lines. This will break any script that imports THIS VERSION.
// (Scripts importing older versions will not be affected.)
//
// runtime.error(_MSG)
// plot(na)
